Returns whether every modifier held in `self` is also held in `other`.

`Modifiers::none()` is a subset of every value, and no value is a subset of `none()` unless
it is `none()` itself.

# Examples

```
# use gpui::Modifiers;
let ctrl_shift = Modifiers::control_shift();
assert!(Modifiers::shift().is_subset_of(&ctrl_shift));
assert!(!Modifiers::alt().is_subset_of(&ctrl_shift));
```

Returns whether the platform's shortcut modifier is held.

This is `platform` (command) on macOS and `control` on Linux and Windows. Use it for
shortcuts such as save and copy, so that they follow each platform's convention.

# Examples

```
# use gpui::Modifiers;
assert!(Modifiers::secondary_key().secondary());
assert!(!Modifiers::shift().secondary());
```

Returns the total length of the run, including the delay.

Returns [`MotionExtent::Infinite`] for [`Motion::repeat_forever`]. Returns `None` only when
a finite total is too large for [`Duration`](std::time::Duration).

# Examples

```
use gpui::{Motion, MotionExtent, millis};

let motion = Motion::new(millis(300)).with_delay(millis(200)).iterations(3);
assert_eq!(motion.checked_extent(), Some(MotionExtent::Finite(millis(1100))));
```

Samples this spring at `elapsed`, starting from rest at zero progress.

Progress is the spring's position, which overshoots when the spring is underdamped. From
the settling time onward the sample is [`MotionPhase::Completed`] at [`Progress::END`],
and it is no longer active.

# Examples

```
use gpui::{Motion, Progress, millis, secs, spring};

let motion = Motion::spring(spring(100., 10., 1.));
assert!(motion.sample(millis(0)).is_active);
let settled = motion.sample(secs(10));
assert!(settled.is_complete());
assert_eq!(settled.progress, Progress::END);
```

Returns every mouse button GPUI knows, in a fixed order.

The order is `Left`, `Right`, `Middle`, `Navigate(Back)` and
`Navigate(Forward)`. Use it to iterate over all buttons, for example to
build a table of handlers.

# Examples

```
use gpui::{MouseButton, NavigationDirection};

assert_eq!(MouseButton::all().len(), 5);
assert_eq!(MouseButton::all()[3], MouseButton::Navigate(NavigationDirection::Back));
```
